WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.527
Week 13: City, Directions, and Public Services. ask for and give directions identify public services confirm a route

2
00:00:08.527 --> 00:00:28.839
Read for the situation. Un visitante busca el museo, pero toma la calle equivocada. Una vecina le indica que siga derecho, cruce la plaza y doble después del correo. A visitor is looking for the museum but takes the wrong street. A neighbor tells him to continue straight, cross the plaza, and turn after the post office.

3
00:00:28.839 --> 00:00:37.579
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:43.184
Reading activities. Reading activity 30; Reading activity 31

5
00:00:43.184 --> 00:00:51.093
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:51.093 --> 00:01:17.073
Model language. Siga derecho hasta la plaza. — Go straight to the plaza. Doble a la izquierda en la segunda esquina. — Turn left at the second corner. ¿Voy bien para el ayuntamiento? — Am I going the right way to city hall? Nos perdimos cerca de la estación. — We got lost near the station. El banco queda enfrente del correo. — The bank is across from the post office.

7
00:01:17.073 --> 00:01:26.993
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
